# Docker Hub

## docker pull

Downloads an image from a container registry.

```bash
docker pull <image_name>:<tag>
```

Examples:

```bash
docker pull ubuntu
docker pull ubuntu:latest
```

If no tag is specified, Docker uses the `latest` tag by default.

---

# docker run

Creates and runs a container from an image.

```bash
docker run <image_name>
```

## Modes of Container Execution

### Foreground / Attached Mode

Default mode.

```bash
docker run ubuntu
docker run ubuntu sleep 20
```

### Background / Detached Mode

```bash
docker run -d ubuntu sleep 20
```

### Interactive Mode

```bash
docker run -it ubuntu bash
```

Exit the container:

```bash
exit
```

