# Port Mapping / Port Binding

Port mapping is used to map a container port to a host port and expose the container service.

```text
-p <host_port>:<container_port>
```

Examples:

```bash
docker run -it -p 8085:8080 tomcat:8.0
docker run -it -p 8086:8080 tomcat:8.0
```

The host port must be unique when multiple containers are running on the same host.

