# Docker Compose

Docker Compose is used to run multiple containers as a service.

* Docker Compose is an extension/plugin for Docker Engine.
* It is used to run multiple containers as a service.
* Docker Compose uses a YAML file to define service configurations.
* Containers that are part of the same service can be managed together.
* Containers can be started and stopped together.

Documentation:

https://docs.docker.com/compose/

---

# Installing Docker Compose

```bash
DOCKER_CONFIG=${DOCKER_CONFIG:-$HOME/.docker}

mkdir -p $DOCKER_CONFIG/cli-plugins

curl -SL https://github.com/docker/compose/releases/download/v2.24.0/docker-compose-linux-x86_64 \
-o $DOCKER_CONFIG/cli-plugins/docker-compose

chmod +x $DOCKER_CONFIG/cli-plugins/docker-compose

docker compose version
```

---

# Docker Compose YAML

YAML files are based on key-value pairs.

Example:

```yaml
services:
  webserv1:
    image: "tomcat:8.0"
    ports:
      - "8098:8080"

  dbserv1:
    image: "redis:alpine"
```

Start the services:

```bash
docker compose up
```

Stop and remove the services:

```bash
docker compose down
```

